desc:Lovers [Arcana synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth drone sequencer arpeggio generative modal scales raga delay chorus phaser shimmer reverb ambient arcana
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument, gfx-voice and gfx-clip (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE LOVERS (card VI of the GFX Arcana series): union, choice, two made one. An LCR spatial union: a PEDAL DRONE
// fixed in the centre, and two spiralling modal sequencers - one hard LEFT, one hard RIGHT - that climb from the drone's
// register in interlocking counter-melodic arpeggios, re-voice themselves round the pedal, trade notes, and court
// each other over minutes; a cross-feedback delay, a modulation send and a shimmer reverb.
// It loads stopped and silent. TRANSPORT (lit by default): REAPER's play / record starts the run and its stop stops
// it; RUN works by hand while REAPER is stopped (free at the project tempo, from the bar). While REAPER plays, every
// step, phrase, reassignment and courtship is reckoned from the song position and the SEED, so a render repeats.
//   PEDAL DRONE  the centre's anchor, never panned: a detuned pair of band-limited saws (DETUNE, 0 - 30 cents), a square
//              an octave down (SUB), a saw a fifth up (FIFTH); TONE (a 12 dB low-pass, 55 Hz - 8 kHz); DRIVE (the house
//              drive: up to +30 dB into the anti-aliased knee clipper, the drive-tracking pre-filter and knee,
//              level-matched); LEVEL; sends to the DELAY, MODULATION and SHIMMER. ROOT (C .. B) and OCTAVE (1 - 4)
//              set the pedal; MIDI sets it too: the lowest key held gives the pedal's note (in the panel's OCTAVE), the
//              ROOT returns when nothing is held. A move of a tone or less glides (GLIDE, 0 - 2 s); a larger one starts
//              a second drone voice on the new note and crossfades the two (over GLIDE, at least 40 ms): no slide, no
//              click. The run swells the drone in (0.7 s) and lets it die away (1.5 s).
//   HARMONY    SCALE: 53 scales in groups - the church modes; minor and major colours (harmonic and melodic minor,
//              harmonic major, Phrygian and Lydian dominant, altered, Lydian augmented, Ukrainian Dorian, Neapolitan
//              major and minor, Hungarian minor and major, double harmonic, Persian, enigmatic, Spanish eight-tone);
//              symmetric (whole tone, both diminished, augmented, Prometheus, tritone); pentatonic and blues; Indian
//              ragas (Bhairav, Todi, Marwa, Kafi, Purvi, Charukesi); Japanese (Hirajoshi, In Sen, Iwato, Kumoi, Yo,
//              Ryukyu); Indonesian (Pelog, Slendro: 12-TET approximations); Ethiopian qenet (Tezeta major and minor,
//              Bati major and minor, Ambassel, Anchihoye: 12-TET approximations - some share their 12-TET shape with a
//              pentatonic or a Japanese scale) - and CUSTOM: twelve lit keys, one octave from the tonic (the tonic is
//              always in); with a library scale they show its notes, and a click starts a CUSTOM scale from it.
//              COUPLING (lit keys): MODE FOLLOWS BASS - the scale is rooted on the pedal and transposes with it; BASS
//              FOLLOWS MODE - the scale keeps its tonic (ROOT) and a new pedal becomes a degree of it: the spirals start
//              from the scale's degree at (or just above) the pedal, re-voiced to sit over the new bass. A new pedal also
//              draws new chordal inversions for both spirals (from the SEED); LOCK keeps the ROOT's own inversions.
//   SPIRALS    two looping sequencers, LEFT (hard left) and RIGHT (hard right, a third above), each on its own grid:
//              RATE (1/4, 1/8 dotted, 1/8, 1/8 triplet, 1/16 dotted, 1/16, 1/16 triplet, 1/32: synced), PATTERN (Up,
//              Down, Up-down: the chord tones - every other degree of the scale; Thirds: up a third, back a step;
//              Broken chord: 1-3-2-4 cells; Scale run; Pendulum: the low tone against a climb; Seeded walk), VOICE.
//              The TWIN GENERATORS (dual-concentric knobs: the OUTER RING sets the LEFT side - drag its rim; the INNER
//              CAP sets the RIGHT - drag the centre; each part has its own hover value, wheel, SHIFT-fine and
//              double-click default): STEPS (3 - 16: unequal lengths interlock), RANGE (1 - 4 octaves), OCTAVE (-1 ..
//              +2), GATE (how long each note is held / rings), TONE, LEVEL, and the DELAY, MOD and SHIMMER sends.
//              ASCENDING INVERSIONS: each completed loop climbs the phrase one chord tone (the next inversion); after
//              TIERS loops (1 - 8) it returns to the base - the last tier fades, the first swells back in, so the wrap
//              is a breath, not a jump. REASSIGN: as a phrase ends its last tier (a new generation) a share of its steps
//              (REASSIGN) is re-assigned to new scale degrees, and some cross-feed - a step takes the other side's note
//              (L's notes migrate to R and back). All from the SEED (NEW draws one, < > step it): the same seed, the
//              same piece. The phrase lanes show each side's loop: a migrated note in the other side's colour, a
//              mirrored or unison one ringed in orange.
//   VOICES     six a side (a note on a busy side takes the quietest voice, faded out in 3 ms first): BELL (a glassy
//              two-operator FM pair, 1 : 3.5; TONE the index, which decays faster than the bell and is held under the
//              band limit), PLUCK (two band-limited saws a few cents apart through a low-pass that opens on the pluck;
//              TONE its height and sweep), MALLET (a struck bar's three modes, 1 : 3.93 : 9.6, the higher ones shorter;
//              TONE the mallet's hardness), PAD (two band-limited saws 10 cents apart, a gentle low-pass, a slow swell).
//   CROSS DELAY  two lines, each feeding back into the OTHER (CROSS 100 %: a full ping-pong mirror) or itself (0 %):
//              SYNC (lit) to a division per side (TIME L, TIME R: 1/16 .. 1 bar) or free (20 ms - 2 s); FEEDBACK
//              (through TONE's damping, a 60 Hz high-pass and a soft limit), TONE, MIX. SHIFT (lit): each tier moves its
//              side's delay to a related time (x 1, dotted, triplet, double, ...: it glides like tape), and as a
//              spiral returns to its base the echoes softly reset (150 ms out, the lines cleared, 150 ms back). IN.
//   MODULATION an analogue-style chorus (7 - 12 ms taps, the right a quarter turn on) into a four-stage phaser (its sweep
//              300 Hz - 3 kHz, a little feedback): RATE, DEPTH, PHASER (how much of it), WIDTH (0 - 200 %: the return's
//              stereo spread), MIX. IN.
//   SHIMMER REVERB  a 24 ms pre-delay, four diffusers, eight long lines (Hadamard); its own sound an octave up (two
//              crossfaded read heads) climbs back into it (SHIMMER), with a lift on the top: SIZE, DECAY (1.5 - 25 s),
//              SHIMMER, MIX. IN. The delay's and the modulation's returns feed it a little.
//   FATE       the series' drift (0 - 100 %, 50 % = the standard amount) as COURTSHIP: the song is cut into four-bar
//              spans, and in some of them (more often with more FATE) the two orbits court - they EXCHANGE notes, trade
//              PANS (cross over and back), trade OCTAVES, MIRROR each other (the right plays the left's figure upside
//              down) or MEET in unison (drawing in towards the centre); then they drift apart again, with a slow sway.
//              0 % = no courtship. The centre drone stays the anchor; the spirals' tuning wanders a touch.
//   VOLUME, LEVEL, SAT (the output soft clip is always on). MIDI: notes (the pedal; channel select), all notes off
//   (CC120 / 123); MIDI passes through.
// The display: a dual-colour phosphor field - the drone's phase portrait as a still figure in the centre, each spiral's
// as an orbit in its own colour (a note rings round, then winds in as it dies) placed where its pan has it, their
// steps round two orbits, the pans along the foot and the courtship now.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc
import gfx-clip.jsfx-inc

